{
 "fps": 30,
 "frames": 1920,
 "dur": 64.0,
 "target": 64.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Mayor Brick's dam was twice as thick as Nell's. It burst first.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.127
  },
  {
   "text": "Right below both dams sat Puddleford: a bakery, a school, and four hundred garden gnomes.",
   "s": 3.327,
   "e": 7.793
  },
  {
   "text": "Brick built his dead straight. \"Straight is strong!\" he said.",
   "s": 7.993,
   "e": 10.637
  },
  {
   "text": "But Nell built hers thin, and bent like a banana.",
   "s": 10.837,
   "e": 12.906
  },
  {
   "text": "Brick laughed so hard his hat fell in the lake.",
   "s": 13.106,
   "e": 15.059
  },
  {
   "text": "Bramble the beaver, who'd built exactly one dam, moved in with Nell. He brought his own pillow.",
   "s": 15.259,
   "e": 20.029
  },
  {
   "text": "Then it rained for nine days, and both lakes rose to the brim.",
   "s": 20.229,
   "e": 23.036
  },
  {
   "text": "It rained so hard, the ducks went indoors.",
   "s": 23.236,
   "e": 25.21
  },
  {
   "text": "Brick's straight dam bulged in the middle, like a belly after dinner.",
   "s": 25.41,
   "e": 28.206
  },
  {
   "text": "\"Straight is strong!\" he yelled, propping it with forty logs. The logs bent too.",
   "s": 28.406,
   "e": 32.197
  },
  {
   "text": "At midnight, the middle popped, and the lake went downtown. A cow surfed by on a sofa.",
   "s": 32.397,
   "e": 36.418
  },
  {
   "text": "Brick's car floated past Brick. It honked.",
   "s": 36.618,
   "e": 38.536
  },
  {
   "text": "But Nell's skinny, bent dam didn't even creak. Why?",
   "s": 38.736,
   "e": 41.103
  },
  {
   "text": "A curve passes the water's push sideways, into the rock walls of the valley.",
   "s": 41.403,
   "e": 44.924
  },
  {
   "text": "It's an arch lying on its side. The harder the water pushes, the tighter it wedges in.",
   "s": 45.324,
   "e": 49.573
  },
  {
   "text": "A straight wall has nothing to lean on, so it bends in the middle and breaks.",
   "s": 49.773,
   "e": 53.329
  },
  {
   "text": "By morning, Puddleford had a brand-new swimming pool. It was Main Street.",
   "s": 53.529,
   "e": 56.941
  },
  {
   "text": "Brick rebuilt his dam, bent like a banana. \"Straight is... strong-ish.\"",
   "s": 57.141,
   "e": 60.718
  },
  {
   "text": "And Bramble got a hard hat: Dam Engineer.",
   "s": 60.838,
   "e": 62.7
  }
 ],
